1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,014
This video helps you prepare for the laboratory assessment, which is ten percent of the course and covers all four outcomes.

2
00:00:09,014 --> 00:00:11,486
It is a general preparation guide.

3
00:00:11,486 --> 00:00:17,592
Follow the instructions and format given by your instructor for the real assessment.

4
00:00:18,392 --> 00:00:22,380
In a lab assessment you work on a dataset with code.

5
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:25,448
The skills tested span the whole course:

6
00:00:25,448 --> 00:00:37,181
describing data, exploring one, two and many variables, cleaning, handling missing values and outliers, encoding, transforming, and interpreting results.

7
00:00:37,181 --> 00:00:41,936
Practise a fixed routine so you never start from a blank page.

8
00:00:42,736 --> 00:00:45,952
Here is the ten-step routine.

9
00:00:45,952 --> 00:00:46,396
One:

10
00:00:46,396 --> 00:00:48,281
load and inspect.

11
00:00:48,281 --> 00:00:48,724
Two:

12
00:00:48,724 --> 00:00:52,717
audit missing values and duplicates.

13
00:00:52,717 --> 00:00:53,382
Three:

14
00:00:53,382 --> 00:00:57,818
convert types and hidden missing values.

15
00:00:57,818 --> 00:00:58,372
Four:

16
00:00:58,372 --> 00:01:01,921
univariate statistics and plots.

17
00:01:01,921 --> 00:01:02,476
Five:

18
00:01:02,476 --> 00:01:03,474
outliers.

19
00:01:03,474 --> 00:01:03,917
Six:

20
00:01:03,917 --> 00:01:06,024
bivariate analysis.

21
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:06,690
Seven:

22
00:01:06,690 --> 00:01:10,571
handle missing values and outliers.

23
00:01:10,571 --> 00:01:11,236
Eight:

24
00:01:11,236 --> 00:01:13,565
encode and transform.

25
00:01:13,565 --> 00:01:14,120
Nine:

26
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:18,112
scale or reduce dimensions if asked.

27
00:01:18,112 --> 00:01:18,556
Ten:

28
00:01:18,556 --> 00:01:21,328
interpret in plain words.

29
00:01:22,128 --> 00:01:25,185
These first lines should be automatic.

30
00:01:25,185 --> 00:01:32,908
Load the file, check the shape and types, preview rows, and count missing values and duplicates.

31
00:01:32,908 --> 00:01:37,413
Add the transposed duplicate check for repeated columns.

32
00:01:37,413 --> 00:01:45,216
Do this every time, because column names, types and row counts change more often than you expect.

33
00:01:46,016 --> 00:01:55,725
For numeric columns, compute mean, median, standard deviation, I Q R, skew and kurtosis in one line each.

34
00:01:55,725 --> 00:02:00,348
Count outliers with the one point five I Q R rule.

35
00:02:00,348 --> 00:02:03,676
Then plot a histogram and a boxplot.

36
00:02:03,676 --> 00:02:04,601
Interpret:

37
00:02:04,601 --> 00:02:09,224
if mean is above median, the tail is on the right.

38
00:02:10,024 --> 00:02:20,106
For relationships, use correlation for two numbers, cross-tabs for two categories, and group by for a number across categories.

39
00:02:20,106 --> 00:02:25,186
Check variance inflation factor before clustering or regression.

40
00:02:25,186 --> 00:02:28,600
Remember that correlation is not causation.

41
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:42,220
For cleaning, convert hidden missing values, fill or impute with a method you can justify, treat outliers by cause, encode categories by type, and transform skewed columns.

42
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:49,152
Put the steps in a pipeline if you will model, so everything is fitted on training rows only.

43
00:02:49,952 --> 00:02:51,379
Manage your time.

44
00:02:51,379 --> 00:02:56,498
Spend the first minutes reading the question and the dataset.

45
00:02:56,498 --> 00:02:59,351
Do the audit before anything else.

46
00:02:59,351 --> 00:03:03,296
Do the compulsory steps first, then the extras.

47
00:03:03,296 --> 00:03:09,757
Comment your code and write one sentence of interpretation after each result.

48
00:03:09,757 --> 00:03:15,632
Leave time to run the notebook from the top, with restart and run all.

49
00:03:16,432 --> 00:03:20,498
Use this self-check before the assessment.

50
00:03:20,498 --> 00:03:24,854
Can you load and audit a dataset from memory?

51
00:03:24,854 --> 00:03:28,242
Describe and plot a numeric column?

52
00:03:28,242 --> 00:03:30,759
Count outliers with I Q R?

53
00:03:30,759 --> 00:03:33,857
Run correlation and a cross-tab?

54
00:03:33,857 --> 00:03:36,858
Impute missing values two ways?

55
00:03:36,858 --> 00:03:39,568
Encode categories correctly?

56
00:03:39,568 --> 00:03:41,892
Log-transform and scale?

57
00:03:41,892 --> 00:03:45,570
And explain each result in a sentence?

58
00:03:45,570 --> 00:03:47,700
If yes, you are ready.

59
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:51,088
Good luck, and thanks for watching.

